#: ../../source/gen-mapping_README.md:3
msgid "Generate source maps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gen-mapping_README.md:5
msgid ""
"`gen-mapping` allows you to generate a source map during transpilation or"
" minification. With a source map, you're able to trace the original "
"location in the source file, either in Chrome's DevTools or using a "
"library like [`@jridgewell/trace-mapping`][trace-mapping]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gen-mapping_README.md:9
msgid ""
"You may already be familiar with the [`source-map`][source-map] package's"
" `SourceMapGenerator`. This provides the same `addMapping` and "
"`setSourceContent` API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gen-mapping_README.md:12
msgid "Installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gen-mapping_README.md:18
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gen-mapping_README.md:67
msgid "Smaller Sourcemaps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gen-mapping_README.md:69
msgid ""
"Not everything needs to be added to a sourcemap, and needless markings "
"can cause signficantly larger file sizes. `gen-mapping` exposes "
"`maybeAddSegment`/`maybeAddMapping` APIs that will intelligently "
"determine if this marking adds useful information. If not, the marking "
"will be skipped."
msgstr ""

